{
 "esm": "1.1.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "geometry",
  "description": "PISM geometry (mass continuity) component (stage 2 of the eqice project): GeometryEvolution::flow_step and GeometryEvolution::source_term_step on the 2-D cartesian grid, plus the pointwise part_grid_threshold_thickness. flow_step integrates the mass-continuity PDE dH/dt = -div(Q), Q = Q_diff + Q_adv, with the exact PISM discretization of GeometryEvolution.cc: the total face flux through each edge is the mask-limited prescribed diffusive flux (the SIA flux qx/qy of the coupled model; here a prescribed Gaussian) plus the mask-limited first-order-upwind advective flux v_face*H_upwind with the iciness-weighted face velocity v_face = (W_c*u_c + W_n*u_n)/max(W_c + W_n, 1); the divergence is the staggered finite-volume stencil divQ = (Q(i,j,0) - Q(i-1,j,0))/dx + (Q(i,j,1) - Q(i,j-1,1))/dy with the zero-flux outer boundary (the mask limiter zeroes every flux on the ice-free outer ring, so the domain sum of divQ telescopes to 0). The Smolarkiewicz-Zalesak non-negativity limiter (make_nonnegative_preserving) and the conservation-error accounting (the bc-mask term dt*divQ and the non-negativity clamps of ensure_nonnegativity) are INACTIVE in this trace -- verified cell by cell: conservation_error = 0 everywhere, so H_change = -dt*divQ exactly and the domain-sum of H_change vanishes to round-off (the closed-domain mass-balance contract). source_term_step is the pointwise map dH_SMB = effective_change(H, dt*smb/rho_ice), dH_BMB = effective_change(H + dH_SMB, -dt*bmr) (with the bc/ocean skip), applied as H_out = H + dH_SMB + dH_BMB, with the effective_change non-negativity clamping; the cell mask and surface after each step follow util/Mask.hh from the updated thickness. The two steps are independent one-year traces from the SAME test-F exact input geometry (flat bed, sea level 0, Mx = My = 31, Lx = Ly = 900 km, 517 grounded-ice + 444 ice-free-bedrock cells), matching stage1/dumps/geometry/columns.csv; the advective velocity, diffusive flux, SMB and basal melt rate are the dumped input fields. The C++ takes one explicit step (forward Euler for flow, an algebraic map for the sources); the harness integrates the flow ODE continuously, so the flow assertions hold the forward-Euler-vs-exact-ODE scheme gap (measured <= 5e-6 relative on H and surface_out and <= 3e-4 on dH_flow at every asserted cell, asserted at rel 1e-5 / 5e-4); the source-step and part-grid reproductions are exact (rel 1e-12). All shared math is imported by reference from ./geometry_templates.esm (the face-flux construction, the mask limiter, the divergence rules, effective_change, cell mask/surface, part_grid_threshold_thickness). Deferred to stage 3: the full geometry-update orchestration (part-grid redistribution, front retreat, mask evolution across steps), the SIA/SSA velocity and SMB/BMB couplings, and the general bc-mask and non-negativity conservation-error branches (documented in the divergence rule and the model descriptions; inactive in this trace).",
  "license": "GPL-3.0-or-later",
  "tags": [
   "eqice:stage2",
   "pism:geometry",
   "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d"
  ]
 },
 "solver": {
  "stiffness": "high",
  "reltol": 1e-08,
  "abstol": 1e-08
 },
 "index_sets": {
  "sample": {
   "kind": "interval",
   "size": 560
  }
 },
