    {
     "_comment": "The mass-continuity PDE dH/dt = -div(Q) with the flux divergence discretized by the rules pism_flow_divergence_x / pism_flow_divergence_y (the staggered stencil (Q(i,j,0) - Q(i-1,j,0))/dx + (Q(i,j,1) - Q(i,j-1,1))/dy with the zero-flux outer boundary; GeometryEvolution::compute_flux_divergence). The conservation-error branch of the C++ (at thickness-bc cells: divQ := 0 and conservation_error += dt*divQ) is inactive here because the bc mask is 0 everywhere; the non-negativity clamp of ensure_nonnegativity is likewise inactive (no cell is drained below zero in this trace), so the C++ result is exactly H_new = H - dt*divQ and the conservation_error vanishes -- documented in the component description.",
