   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "flow_step_one_year",
     "description": "One dt = 1 year flow step from the test-F exact geometry with the dumped forcing (u, v, qx, qy, mask; stage1/dumps/geometry/columns.csv): H at t = dt reproduces the dumped H_out_flow and dH_flow at the asserted cells (dome, mid-radius, margin, the ice-free margin ring cells that gain ice and flip mask 0 -> 2, and ice-free cells). The C++ takes one forward-Euler step; the harness integrates the mass-continuity ODE continuously, so the asserted agreement carries the forward-Euler-vs-exact-ODE scheme gap (measured <= 5e-6 relative on H and surface_out and <= 3e-4 on dH_flow at every asserted cell; dominated by the advective coupling, since the diffusive flux is prescribed and constant, making the diffusive part of the discrete step exact). The closed-domain mass-balance contract of the C++ trace (sum(H_change) = sum(conservation_error) = 0 to round-off, since the flux limiters zero every flux on the ice-free outer ring and SMB = BMB = 0) is asserted as the domain integral (sum) of dH_flow at abs 1e-10 m (measured -3.3e-12 m: the residual of the ODE integration on the closed domain, whose telescoping divergence sum the C++ trace carries to round-off ~1e-15 m) and as min(H) >= 0 at abs 1e-10 m (measured exactly 0: the non-negativity the C++ limiter and clamp protect).",
     "time_span": {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 31556925.9747
     },
     "assertions": [
      {
